{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>מזי רעב (the wasting of hunger).</b> Like שרופי רעב (scorched by hunger), from the root of למזא לאתונא (to fodder the she-ass)." "<b>ולחומי רשף (and the fierce heat of reshef).</b> A species of bird, like ובני רשף יגביהו עוף (and the sons of reshef raise flight). But the correct view in my eyes is that He mentioned the four evil judgments, and they are: famine — and this is מזי רעב; ולחומי רשף וקטב מרירי — this is pestilence; ושן בהמות — אשלח בם חיה (I will send among them the beast); וחרב מחוץ — תשכל חרב (the sword shall bereave). And so the meaning of רשף will be like רשפיה רשפי אש (its sparks, sparks of fire), and the sense is that the air becomes hot." "<b>וקטב (and qetev).</b> Like הכרתה (cutting off)." "<b>מרירי (meriri).</b> Bitterness in the air, like כמרירי יום (like the bitterness of day). And so it is written מקטב ישוד צהרים (the destruction that wastes at noon) — like pestilence. ולחומי רשף — like a species, and so many interpret." "<b>עם חמת זוחלי עפר (with the venom of creeping things of dust).</b> To bite, and חמה (venom/heat) is a term for biting." "And the meaning of <b>עפר (dust)</b> is like the fiery serpents, and the word זוחלי (creeping things) [implies] fear, for everyone who sees them fears them, in the sense of terror — for there is an adjective of a noun and its parallel in the passage of Elihu son of Barachel."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:09.424026083Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}